Most calculators support both fractional odds (traditional UK format such as 5/1 or 11/4) and decimal odds (European format like 6.00 or 3.75), converting automatically for total return computation. Fractional odds display profit relative to stake, while decimal odds include the stake within the quoted figure. Players accustomed to UK betting conventions typically enter fractional values, which the Heinz Flag Calculator converts internally for multiplication across accumulator legs. The system must also handle Dead Heat rules where two or more selections tie, reducing returns by dividing stake among tied outcomes. When a selection is declared Void due to non-runner status, the calculator removes that leg and recalculates remaining valid combinations at reduced bet counts.
