## Heinz Flag vs Standard Heinz - Key Differences
The standard Heinz contains 57 bets from 6 selections, while the Heinz Flag extends this to 87 bets by adding 30 Single Stakes About (SSA) Pairs. This fundamental structural difference increases both stake cost and potential coverage. A Heinz comprises 15 doubles, 20 trebles, 15 four-folds, 6 five-folds, and 1 six-fold accumulator. The Heinz Flag Calculator incorporates these same 57 combinations plus the additional SSA Pairs component, which creates conditional double bets across all selection pairings.
The stake differential represents a significant consideration for bankroll management. At £1 per bet, a standard Heinz costs £57 total stake, whereas a Heinz Flag requires £87. This £30 premium purchases the SSA Pairs coverage, which pays returns if any two selections win regardless of other outcomes. The standard Heinz demands at least two winners to generate returns through its doubles, but offers no single-selection protection. The Heinz Flag provides the same accumulator upside while adding safety bets that activate with just two successful picks.
