In a scenario where three selections win, the returns come from winning doubles and trebles. Three winners generate three winning doubles (3 combinations of 2 from 3 winners) and one winning treble. If Arsenal, Liverpool, and Manchester City win, the returns include doubles combining these three teams plus the single treble. At the stated odds, this partial success recovers a portion of the stake but typically results in an overall loss, illustrating the bet's high-risk nature.
When four selections win, the coverage expands significantly. Four winners produce six winning doubles (combinations of 2 from 4), four winning trebles (combinations of 3 from 4), and one four-fold accumulator. The SSA Pairs within the Heinz structure also contribute returns. This scenario often moves closer to break-even or modest profit, depending on the odds.
